==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|þul-|lang=ang}}, a weak grade of {{proto|Indo-European|tel-, tol-, tl-|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|þolian|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|dolon|dolōn}}, Old Norse {{term|þola}} (Swedish {{term|tåla}}), Gothic {{term|𐌸𐌿𐌻𐌰𐌽}}; compare Latin {{term|tuli}}, {{term|tolerare||tolerate}}, {{term|tollere||lift up, bear}}, Ancient Greek {{term|τλῆναι|sc=polytonic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/θoliɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
'''þolian'''

# to [[suffer]], [[endure]]

